    <div class="itdgl-clinic-intro">
      <p>Website + online booking + WhatsApp Cloud API integration for a dermatology clinic in Nagpur, Maharashtra is the operational foundation for patient acquisition. Weak website + no booking = leaked leads. Modern clinic website: mobile-first + Core Web Vitals + doctor + procedure + before-after + reviews + booking + WhatsApp button + directions + local schema. This FAQ answers 12 questions Nagpur dermatologists ask about clinic website + booking + WhatsApp.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="itdgl-evidence-band">
      <strong>ITD CLINIC MARKETING &mdash; WHAT WE ACTUALLY DO:</strong>
      ITD GrowthLabs runs full-stack digital marketing for dermatology + skincare clinics across Thane, Mumbai, Navi Mumbai, Dombivli, Kalyan, Nagpur, Nashik, and Pune. Social media management + Reels + viral content, Meta + Google ads, website + online booking + WhatsApp Cloud API integration, Google Business Profile optimisation + local SEO, and patient lead generation. We work with clinics that don't have in-house marketing teams — treating the marketing function as an outsourced growth partner, not a vendor. Every answer below reflects live clinic work.
    </div>

    <div class="itdgl-faq-list" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What does a modern dermatology clinic website in Nagpur include?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">(1) Mobile-first design (Core Web Vitals green — LCP <2.5s, FID <100ms, CLS <0.1), (2) Homepage with doctor + facility + hero procedures + reviews + book-now CTA, (3) Doctor profile pages with credentials + specialisation + Google reviews, (4) Procedure pages (HydraFacial + laser + peels + Botox + acne + pigmentation) with before-after (compliance-safe) + FAQ + pricing range, (5) Before-after gallery (categorised by procedure + with consent + disclaimer), (6) Booking system integrated with clinic calendar, (7) WhatsApp Cloud API button (always-visible float), (8) Google Maps + directions + parking + landmarks (Civil Lines + Dhantoli + Ramdaspeth + Sitabuldi + Wardha Road), (9) LocalBusiness + MedicalBusiness + FAQ + Article schema, (10) Blog/education section (SEO + AI search citation). In Nagpur with Marathi + Hindi + English, multilingual support (Marathi + Hindi + English).</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How much does a dermatology clinic website cost in Nagpur?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Boutique (WordPress + booking + WhatsApp): Rs 60,000-1,50,000 one-time (3-5 weeks). Mid-market (custom design + advanced booking + AR try-on for facial procedures + payments): Rs 1,50,000-3,50,000 (5-8 weeks). Enterprise (multi-location + multi-doctor + advanced booking + patient portal + electronic health record integration): Rs 3,50,000-8,00,000+ (8-14 weeks). Post-launch maintenance + updates + hosting Rs 15,000-60,000/month. Bundled with marketing retainer typical.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What booking system integrations work for a Nagpur dermatology clinic?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Popular: Cliniify (dedicated clinic management), Practo (marketplace + booking), Bookinginfo, custom Shopify/Woo booking. Key features: doctor availability calendar sync, procedure/service selection, consultation type (in-person + video), automated confirmation + reminder SMS + WhatsApp, follow-up reminder, patient record. Integration with Google Calendar + WhatsApp Cloud API + clinic EMR/EHR essential.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How does WhatsApp Cloud API integration work for a Nagpur dermatology clinic?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Website WhatsApp button → clicks open WhatsApp with pre-filled message → Interakt/AiSensy Cloud API handles: welcome + qualifying questions (concern + location + budget + preferred time) + booking calendar link + doctor availability + directions + reminder + post-consultation follow-up. Automated flows for common inquiries. Human handoff for complex questions within 15 min business hours. Cost: Rs 3-15K/month tooling + per-message (Rs 0.30-2 per message).</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">Should we use WordPress, Shopify, or custom for a dermatology clinic website?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">WordPress + booking plugin (Amelia + Bookly + native) — most common + cost-effective. Rs 60K-1.5L build. Right for solo + 2-3 doctor clinics. Shopify (with booking apps like BookThatApp) — right if adding e-commerce (skincare product sales) alongside consultation booking. Rs 1-3L build. Custom (React/Next.js + backend) — Rs 3-8L build. Right for multi-location + advanced patient portal + EMR integration. For most Nagpur dermatology clinics, WordPress + strong plugin stack sufficient.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What Core Web Vitals + SEO essentials for Nagpur dermatology clinic websites?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Core Web Vitals green: LCP <2.5s (image + video optimisation + CDN), FID <100ms (minimal blocking JS), CLS <0.1 (fixed dimensions + no layout shifts). SEO: mobile-first indexing, LocalBusiness + MedicalBusiness + FAQPage + Article schema, Nagpur-specific landing pages, procedure-specific SEO pages, blog for AI search citation, HTTPS + secure + fast. In Nagpur, Marathi + Hindi content pages for regional SEO catchment.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How do we handle before-after gallery + patient consent on a dermatology website?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Signed consent form per patient — named use (website + Instagram + Facebook + YouTube + all future marketing). Before-after gallery: same lighting + angle + time + no filters + minimum 4-week interval + individual-results-may-vary disclaimer overlay + patient-consent-obtained badge. Category filters (acne + pigmentation + laser + Botox + procedures). Consent revocable — patient can request removal any time. In Nagpur, Maharashtra Medical Council + Maharashtra FDA + NMC (Nagpur Municipal Corporation) + ethical marketing enforcement.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What booking conversion rate is realistic for a Nagpur dermatology clinic website?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Well-executed dermatology website: 4-9% booking-inquiry conversion rate on paid traffic, 6-12% on organic + GMB traffic. First-time visitor: 2-5%. Returning visitor: 8-15%. Referral traffic: 10-20%. Key drivers: clear procedure pricing + before-after + doctor credentials + reviews + easy booking + WhatsApp button + multilingual + fast site.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How do we integrate reviews + testimonials on a dermatology website?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Google Business Profile reviews embedded (auto-updated). Judge.me / Yotpo / Trustpilot integrated if using e-commerce. Patient testimonials with signed consent form + verified purchase/consultation. Text + video testimonials. Review generation programme via post-consultation WhatsApp + email + SMS (asks for Google review within 24-48hrs of visit). Target 30-100 Google reviews/year for competitive Nagpur clinic.</div>
      </div>
